<title>USA: Ithaca College, N.Y., bonds repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>Ithaca College, N.Y., bonds repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Albany Corp said Tuesday it repriced Dormitory Authority of the State of New York's $42 million bond issue for Ithaca College, lowering yields in several maturities and cutting the top yield in 2026 to 5.61 percent from 5.65 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>DORMITORY AUTHORITY OF THE STATE OF NEW YORK</p>
<p>RE: $42,060,000*</p>
<p>ITHACA COLLEGE</p>
<p>INSURED REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1997</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>NOTE THE PRICE CHANGE 2000-2007 AND 2026.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 02/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>07/01/1998		  120M    3.70  %	100.00</p>
<p>07/01/1999		  125M    4.50  %	  4.00</p>
